# Copy to `.to-done/secrets` in the repo you are running against, fill in one
# value per group, and `chmod 600` it. This file is the only place to-done
# reads credentials from. Keep it gitignored.

# Fine-grained PAT, this repo only: Issues R/W, Pull requests R/W,
# Contents R/W, Metadata R. Nothing else, and nothing cross-repo.
GH_TOKEN=

# Claude, pick one. `claude setup-token` mints the subscription token; the API
# key bills per token, and a long run is a lot of tokens. Only the one you
# set reaches the container, so an expired token fails the phase instead of
# quietly falling back to metered billing.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Codex, required by the review phase and available to every other one.
# The loop reads `~/.codex/auth.json` itself, fresh, as each container starts,
# and the review refuses to run if that credential has expired. Keep the host
# login healthy with `codex login` and this section needs no attention.
#
# Set CODEX_AUTH_FILE only if your auth.json is somewhere else, for example
# because you set a different CODEX_HOME. A path, never the file's contents.
# CODEX_AUTH_FILE=~/.codex/auth.json
#
# Set OPENAI_API_KEY instead to run the cross-check on metered API billing and
# skip the host login entirely. When it is set it wins, and every run bills.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
